<http://www.ebu.ch/metadata/ontologies/ebucore/ebucore> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/description> "Guidelines: for the purpose of flexibility and interoperability with a wider range of implementations, some properties purposefully do not have a range and accept either a resource or a literal.  When a resource is used, it is recommended to reuse objects defined in the model (e.g. pair hasEvent/Event or hasRole/Role). Example 1: x hasRole 'actor'. Example 2: x hasRole _:Role_1 (a reference to the Concept Id from a SKOS Role vocabulary defined in the ontology)."@en .
