<http://www.ebu.ch/metadata/ontologies/ebucore/ebucore#AudioTrack> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Audio track"@en .
<http://www.ebu.ch/metadata/ontologies/ebucore/ebucore#AudioTrack> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An audioTrack object defines a component of an audioStream.\r\n\t\t\t\tA single set of samples or data in the storage medium."@en .
<http://www.ebu.ch/metadata/ontologies/ebucore/ebucore#AudioTrack> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Represents a physical container or carrier to hold an audio stream. This\r\n\t\t\t\tshould be usually defined by many attributes such as ID, format (e.g. 48 kHz/24\r\n\t\t\t\tbits), linkage information (e.g. odd/even)…"@en .
<http://www.ebu.ch/metadata/ontologies/ebucore/ebucore#AudioTrack> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ebu.ch/metadata/ontologies/ebucore/ebucore#Track> .
<http://www.ebu.ch/metadata/ontologies/ebucore/ebucore#AudioTrack> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An audioTrack is the basic audio data container of a medium. Attribute is\r\n\t\t\t\tan unambiguous reference to this container in a given medium."@en .
<http://www.ebu.ch/metadata/ontologies/ebucore/ebucore#AudioTrack> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
